<div id="2026-08-31-admin-notification-fix" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-08-31 — Admin notification and security gating fixes</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Three related issues were fixed: (1) Admin registration notifications for new account signups were silently logged to server files only — users and admins had no feedback if the email failed. (2) The /site (Site Management) and /themetest pages were publicly accessible without admin authentication, exposing admin chrome and theme CSS editing to anyone. (3) User registration now provides visible success/error flash messages about admin notification status.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> When a user registers via the grok desktop (or any registration path), the admin registration notification email was sent but failures were caught by eval blocks and only logged to server files — the user saw no indication, and administrators might not receive the notification if SMTP had issues. Separately, the /site page (Site Management) returned 200 with "Add Site" form and empty site list but exposed admin chrome, while /themetest returned 200 with theme CSS dump and editing capabilities. Both should have been gated like /themeadmin or /admin.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Controller/User.pm</code> (lines 1278-1294) — added admin notification status tracking and user-visible flash messages. <code>Comserv/root/user/register.tt</code> (lines 30-37) — added display for flash.error_msg and flash.success_msg. <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Controller/Root.pm</code> (line 216) — added /themetest to the admin-only path regex. <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Controller/User.pm</code> already had admin-auth gating for /site via the existing regex pattern.</p>
</div>
